{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And I will take you to Me for a people</b> — when you come to Mount Sinai and receive the Torah, for there it is stated (Exodus 19:5), \"and you shall be to Me a treasured possession.\"" "And the sense of <b>and you shall know that I am YHWH your Elohim who brings you out from under the burdens of Egypt</b> — Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 6:7) said that it was in the arrangement of the great compendium for the exalted ministers that they would yet remain in exile. But this is not the way of the interpretation; rather, He says: when I redeem you with an outstretched arm, which all the nations shall see, you shall know that I am YHWH who performs signs and wonders renewed in the world, and I am your Elohim, and it is for your sake that I have done this, for you are the portion of HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:03:33.366949065Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}